0..78 Comment "// A record type\'s faces refused: one face holds a label the record lacks, and"
79..157 Comment "// one face is named twice. An extension type is refused when it names a field"
158..234 Comment "// or a face that the record type lacks. Another fixes a field at a value of"
235..310 Comment "// another type. A record literal at a patched type states a fixed field at"
311..388 Comment "// another value, and so does a configuration coerced in to a patched type. A"
389..465 Comment "// system of faces names one face twice, and another system\'s faces disagree"
466..485 Comment "// where they meet."
486..488 Comment "//"
489..568 Comment "// A face lists only labels its record holds, and each face has its own name. A"
569..646 Comment "// reader `.#{` fixes only the fields its record type writes, and a face only"
647..725 Comment "// when the type member names it. A face\'s refusal covers its record and marks"
726..803 Comment "// the label, and the others stand at the second name or at the face. A fixed"
804..883 Comment "// value has its field\'s type, and a fixed field holds its reader\'s value. Each"
884..959 Comment "// of the two refusals stands at the value, the field or the configuration."
960..962 Comment "//"
963..1039 Comment "// The types stand in a module, whose members carry the verdict each refusal"
1040..1114 Comment "// states. Each refusal names the face and the record type. Two faces of a"
1115..1195 Comment "// system agree on their meet, and the refusal stands at the later face\'s value."
1196..1198 Comment "//"
1199..1280 Comment "// - see: `model/desc/record-faces.gandr` — the faces read, and the reader read"
1281..1362 Comment "// - see: `pathological/desc/shaped-signature.gandr` — a theory\'s faces refused"
1363..1373 Comment "//   alike"
1374..1440 Comment "// - see: #6504 — faces on lazy records and codata declarations."
1442..1506 Comment "/// Two record types, each with a faces block the check refuses."
